e. But if they don’t have the 2, then I take the lead and can follow with my pairs.  \n\nIf I **play Red Joker**, it’s guaranteed to win the trick, but wastes rocket on a free play when I might need it later to stop a bomb or finish.  \n\n**Best move:** Start with ♣A.  \nIt forces the Previous Player to use the last 2 if they have it (which would make them win, but that’s a risk I must take; playing a lower card also risks them having any single higher than that card, which they likely do given they held back). But based on card counting, the last 2 might be with Next Player. This is the safest high single to pressure opponents without wasting the rocket.  \n\n---\n\n**Reason:**  \nChoosing ♣A maximizes control without burning the most powerful card (Red Joker). It pressures Previous Player’s last card — if they can’t beat it, I regain initiative and can continue with pairs. If they can beat it, they’d need the last 2, which isn’t certain. Starting lower risks letting them win with a middle card (like a Q, which is still available), while starting higher wastes a trump unnecessarily.  \n\n---\n\n**Answer:** {"cards": ["♣A"]}'}
